# Per-client topic permissions.
#
# With an acl_file configured, an authenticated user gets NO access unless
# something below grants it. Each device is confined to its own prefix so a
# compromised client cannot drive the others - a garage door opener has no
# business publishing camera commands.

# --- camera service -------------------------------------------------------
# Owns everything under camera/. It also serves the dashboard today, so it
# needs to see the other devices and issue commands to them - but only on
# their /set topics, never their state.
user camera
topic readwrite camera/#
topic read garage/#
topic write garage/+/set
topic read hvac/#
topic write hvac/+/set

# --- ratgdo garage controller (user created when the hardware arrives) ----
user ratgdo
topic readwrite garage/#

# --- Z-Wave JS gateway (user created when the dongle arrives) -------------
user zwave
topic readwrite hvac/#
